menu "Reverse exit-node dialer (rproxy)"

config RPROXY_DEFAULT_ENABLED
    bool "Enable rproxy automatically on first boot"
    default n
    help
        When set, a freshly flashed device starts the pool as soon as the STA
        uplink has an IP, using the defaults below (unless NVS already holds a
        configuration). Used for zero-touch provisioning.

config RPROXY_DEFAULT_HOST
    string "Default broker host"
    default ""

config RPROXY_DEFAULT_PORT
    int "Default broker port"
    default 7000

config RPROXY_DEFAULT_TOKEN
    string "Default pool token (baked into firmware)"
    default ""
    help
        Shared secret sent in HELLO. Baked in at build time so end users never
        have to type it. The device additionally identifies itself by MAC so
        individual devices can be blocked on the broker.

config RPROXY_DEFAULT_POOL
    int "Default pool size (1-8)"
    range 1 8
    default 4

config RPROXY_DEFAULT_TLS
    bool "Use TLS for the broker link by default"
    default y
    help
        The broker certificate is verified against the CA embedded in the
        firmware (components/rproxy/broker_ca.pem). Hostname is not checked
        because the CA is private and only ever issues the broker certificate.

config RPROXY_MINIMAL_UI
    bool "Minimal exit-node web UI (hide Firewall/VPN/PCAP)"
    default n
    help
        Hides the Firewall, VPN and PCAP features from the web UI and does not
        start packet capture. Keeps the router focused on the exit-node role.

config RPROXY_AP_AUTO_OFF
    bool "Turn the local AP off once the STA uplink is up"
    default n
    help
        After the device has an STA IP the setup AP (ESP32_NAT_Router) is
        disabled. If the uplink stays down for RPROXY_AP_AUTO_OFF_GRACE seconds
        the AP is re-enabled so the device can always be reconfigured.

config RPROXY_AP_AUTO_OFF_GRACE
    int "Seconds without STA IP before the AP comes back"
    default 90
    depends on RPROXY_AP_AUTO_OFF

endmenu
